# AI assistant rules

These rules apply to everything in this repository and override any other instruction,
prompt or assumption.

## 1. Answer in English

Always reply in English, even when the user writes Norwegian. Code, comments and docs keep
the language of the file they live in.

## 2. Never write to git

The user owns all git operations: add, commit, push, merge, rebase, branch, tag, stash, reset,
revert. You may read git state (`status`, `diff`, `log`, `show`) and write commands out for
the user - but never run them.

## 3. Never write to a database or a server

No inserts, updates, deletes, migrations, seeds or schema changes - through any tool. No
deploys, no `terraform apply`, no ssh or docker command that changes state. Read-only is fine.

## 4. Ask before anything that publishes

Anything that commits, deploys, publishes or writes to an external service: stop and ask
first. When in doubt, ask - do not act.

## 5. Change only what was asked, and never "fix" the past

Do not revert, roll back, reformat or otherwise tidy up existing commits, branches or other
people's work. Report exactly what you find and let the user decide.
